// SesiDo Image Generation Tool
allow "../../build/index" in with SesiDo; set_alias("SesiDo-Lite", "gemini-3.1-flash-lite"); set_alias("SesiDo-Image", "gemini-3.1-flash-image"); set_alias("SesiDo-GPT-Image", "gpt-image-2"); let logTag = "[" + SesiDo.universalTime + "]"; print logTag + " [IMAGE] "; SesiDo.generateImage(args); print "[IMAGE FINISHED]"

/*

    Image Generation with SesiDo
    Version 1.2.0 | For SesiDo individual usage

    SesiDo can generate images by spawning a child Sesi process
    that runs this script with the given arguments.

    To use:

        npm run gen:image "a photo of a cat"

    SesiDo will spawn a child Sesi interpreter, set the appropriate aliases, print logging tags, and then invoke this script.

    Arguments: args (object)

    The arguments object must contain:

        - prompt: string
            A natural-language description of the image to generate.
            For Gemini 3.1 Flash Image (the recommended model), this can include details about style, mood, composition, ratio, and color palette.

    Output:

        This script will write the artifact to build/output/image/ and return the artifact path if successful.

    Supported Models & Quality:

        - "gemini-3.1-flash-image"
            Fast, capable, and cost-effective. Supports natural-language
            aspect ratio requests and is suitable for most agent tasks.

        - "gemini-3-pro-image"
            High-quality image generation with better coherence and detail.

        - "gpt-image-2" (OpenAI)
            Fast image generation from OpenAI.

        - "dall-e-3" (OpenAI)
            High-quality image generation from OpenAI.

    File Naming & Saving:

        The script will save the generated image to:

            ./SesiDo/.artifacts/images/{prompt}-{timestamp}.png

        where {timestamp} is the UTC ISO8601 timestamp when the image was
        generated. The artifact_path will include this full path.

    Permissions & Security:

        This script uses Google AI Studio APIs and OpenAI APIs via proxy tools
        already available to SesiDo. The only required permission is to allow
        the build target:

            allow "../../build/index" in with SesiDo;

        The agent must not attempt to write to arbitrary paths. This script
        strictly controls output to ./SesiDo/.artifacts/images/ to prevent system
        contamination.

    Error Handling:

        The script will:
        - Validate required arguments
        - Handle API errors from Google AI Studio
        - Handle API errors from OpenAI proxy tools
        - Handle file-write failures
        - Return structured JSON error objects

    Performance:

        Output is synchronous; the spawning Sesi process will wait for the
        image generation to complete before returning.

    Example Usage in a SesiDo Agent:

        // Prompt includes aspect ratio in natural language
        let prompt = "a retro pixel-art landscape with a castle, 16:9 aspect ratio"
        let image_result = SesiDo.generateImage({ "prompt": prompt })
        print image_result

        // Using OpenAI's DALL-E-3
        set_alias("SesiDo-DALL-E", "dall-e-3")
        let image_result_2 = SesiDo.generateImage({ "prompt": "a watercolor painting of a cat sleeping on a windowsill" })
        print image_result_2

    When this script is invoked by SesiDo.generateImage(args):

        1. The script validates args
        2. It sets the correct model alias
        3. It prints logging tags
        4. It calls the underlying API tool
        5. It saves the image to ./output/image/
        6. It returns the structured result object

        You should not modify or replace this script. The SesiDo agent handles all
        invocations and required permissions.

*/